# Docs Package (`packages/docs`)

## Auth and deployment (Vercel)

- **Disable auth**: Set `DOCS_AUTH_DISABLED=true` to skip GitHub OAuth — middleware allows all. Use locally and on Vercel Preview; use `false` or unset on production.
- **OAuth flow**: When auth is enabled, Edge middleware (`middleware.ts`) redirects unauthenticated users to `/api/auth/login`; callback is `api/auth/callback.ts` (exchange code, optional contributor check, set JWT cookie).
- **Contributor check**: If `GITHUB_REPO_OWNER` and `GITHUB_REPO_NAME` are set (and a repo token is present), only the repo owner and users listed in `GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/contributors` can log in. Repo owner is always allowed even if not in the list.
- **Env**: Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill for local OAuth testing or when running against Vercel-like config. Do not commit `.env`. When adding or changing auth-related env vars, update `.env.example` and `docs/vercel-github-oauth.mdx`.

## Structure

- `api/` — Vercel serverless routes (auth login/callback/logout).
- `lib/auth.ts` — JWT session helpers (Edge-compatible; uses dynamic `import('jose')`).
- `middleware.ts` — Vercel Edge Middleware; protects all routes except `/api/auth/` and static assets.
